  "caveats": [
    "Latencies are measured against scratch copies that hold no RLS policy and no join to chunks, and are taken while the scratch schema is competing for 128 MB of shared_buffers with the production corpus. They are comparable to each other and not to ef-search.json or latency.json.",
    "pgvector raises the effective ef_search to the query's LIMIT, so a rescore width above hnsw_ef_search widens the graph walk as well as the shortlist. Part of the cost of a wide rescore is that, not the rescore alone.",
    "Binary quantisation shrinks the index, not the table. Rescoring reads the fp32 vectors from the heap, so the storage saving is in what has to stay resident, which is the constraint this measurement is about.",
    "Nothing here tests a corpus in a different language mix, and nothing tests index build time at the scale that decides the question."
  ],
